{"subjectId":"cpp","id":"strings","title":"std::string","group":"Pointers, Arrays & Strings","order":24,"html":"<p class=\"lead\"><code>std::string</code> is a growable, owning sequence of <code>char</code> with value semantics — copying a string copies its characters. Forget <code>char*</code> for text.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-code\"></i>Create, combine, access</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;cctype&gt;\n#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n\nint main() {\n    std::string a = \"Hello\";\n    std::string b(3, '!');              // \"!!!\"\n    std::string c = a + \", world\" + b;  // concatenation\n    c += '?';\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; c &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; c.size() &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; c[0] &lt;&lt; c.front() &lt;&lt; c.back() &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; c.at(4) &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; std::boolalpha &lt;&lt; c.empty() &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; (a == \"Hello\") &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; (a &lt; \"Help\") &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    for (char&amp; ch : a) ch = static_cast&lt;char&gt;(std::toupper(static_cast&lt;unsigned char&gt;(ch)));\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; a &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>Hello, world!!!? 16\nHH? o\nfalse true true\nHELLO</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-search\"></i>Search &amp; modify</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n\nint main() {\n    std::string s = \"the quick brown fox\";\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; s.find(\"quick\") &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; s.find('o') &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; s.rfind('o') &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    if (s.find(\"cat\") == std::string::npos) std::cout &lt;&lt; \"no cat\\n\";\n\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; s.substr(4, 5) &lt;&lt; '|' &lt;&lt; s.substr(16) &lt;&lt; '\\n';   // substr(pos, count)\n    s.replace(4, 5, \"slow\");                                      // replace(pos, count, text)\n    s.insert(0, \"&gt;&gt; \");\n    s.erase(s.size() - 4);                                        // erase from pos to end\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; s &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; s.starts_with(\"&gt;&gt;\") &lt;&lt; s.ends_with(\"brown\") &lt;&lt; '\\n';  // C++20\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>4 12 17\nno cat\nquick|fox\n&gt;&gt; the slow brown\n11</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Call</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Length</td><td><code>s.size()</code> / <code>s.length()</code></td><td>O(1)</td></tr><tr><td>Find</td><td><code>s.find(x, pos)</code>, <code>rfind</code>, <code>find_first_of</code></td><td>Returns index or <code>std::string::npos</code></td></tr><tr><td>Substring</td><td><code>s.substr(pos, len)</code></td><td>Returns a <em>new</em> string (copy)</td></tr><tr><td>Modify</td><td><code>+=</code>, <code>push_back</code>, <code>pop_back</code>, <code>insert</code>, <code>erase</code>, <code>replace</code>, <code>clear</code></td><td>Amortised O(1) append</td></tr><tr><td>Compare</td><td><code>==</code>, <code>&lt;</code>, <code>s.compare(t)</code></td><td>Lexicographic</td></tr><tr><td>Prefix/suffix</td><td><code>starts_with</code>, <code>ends_with</code> (C++20), <code>contains</code> (C++23)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>C string</td><td><code>s.c_str()</code></td><td>Null-terminated <code>const char*</code> for C APIs</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-transform\"></i>Numbers ↔ strings</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n\nint main() {\n    int n = std::stoi(\"42\");\n    double d = std::stod(\"3.5\");\n    long long big = std::stoll(\"9000000000\");\n    std::string s = std::to_string(n + 1) + \"/\" + std::to_string(big);\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; n * 2 &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; d * 2 &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; s &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; std::stoi(\"ff\", nullptr, 16) &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; std::stoi(\"  12abc\") &lt;&lt; '\\n';   // base 16; stops at non-digits\n    try { std::cout &lt;&lt; std::stoi(\"abc\"); } catch (const std::invalid_argument&amp;) { std::cout &lt;&lt; \"invalid\\n\"; }\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>84 7 43/9000000000\n255 12\ninvalid</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-separator\"></i>Splitting and joining</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;sstream&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n#include &lt;vector&gt;\n\nstd::vector&lt;std::string&gt; split(const std::string&amp; s, char delim) {\n    std::vector&lt;std::string&gt; parts;\n    std::stringstream ss(s);\n    std::string item;\n    while (std::getline(ss, item, delim)) parts.push_back(item);\n    return parts;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    auto parts = split(\"red,green,,blue\", ',');\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; parts.size() &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    std::string joined;\n    for (std::size_t i = 0; i &lt; parts.size(); ++i) joined += (i ? \" | \" : \"\") + parts[i];\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; joined &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>4\nred | green |  | blue</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">SSO</div><p>Small strings (≈ up to 15–22 chars depending on the library) are stored <em>inside</em> the string object — the <strong>small string optimisation (SSO)</strong> — so no heap allocation happens for them.</p></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p><code>s + 'a' + 'b'</code> is fine, but <code>\"abc\" + \"def\"</code> doesn't compile (two pointers), and <code>\"abc\" + 1</code> compiles to pointer arithmetic (<code>\"bc\"</code>)! Make one side a <code>std::string</code>: <code>std::string(\"abc\") + \"def\"</code> or <code>\"abc\"s + \"def\"</code>.</p></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What does std::string::npos mean?</summary><div><p>It's the largest value of <code>std::size_t</code> (<code>static_cast&lt;size_t&gt;(-1)</code>). Search functions return it to mean “not found”, and <code>substr</code>/<code>erase</code> accept it as “until the end”.</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Is std::string null-terminated?</summary><div><p>Since C++11, <code>s.c_str()</code> and <code>s.data()</code> are guaranteed to point to a null-terminated buffer and <code>s[s.size()]</code> is <code>'\\0'</code>. But a <code>std::string</code> may also contain embedded <code>'\\0'</code> characters, and <code>size()</code> doesn't count the terminator.</p></div></details></section>"}